('This checks only direct imports.', 'This small example checks direct absolute import statements, requires at least one source file, and matches the top-level package exactly. It does not resolve relative or dynamic imports and can include imports guarded by TYPE_CHECKING.'),
('Big-bang rewrites have a poor track record. Joel Spolsky\'s essay *Things You Should Never Do* uses Netscape\'s ground-up rewrite, which took about three years while competitors moved ahead, as the cautionary tale.', 'A long all-at-once rewrite can delay feedback and lose undocumented behavior. Joel Spolsky\'s essay Things You Should Never Do argues against this approach using Netscape as a cautionary example.\n\n> [!note] Evidence gap\n> A universal rewrite failure rate and a precise single-cause Netscape chronology are omitted; an opinion essay is not sufficient evidence for those claims.'),
