def adr(q):
 q[2]['options'][2]['explanation']='The aim is incremental replacement while serving users. Data migration and side effects can make particular steps hard to reverse; routing alone does not prove safety.'
 q[3]['options'][3]['explanation']='Small changes avoid a single long-diverged merge, but compatibility tests, green builds and data-safe rollback still require explicit work.'
 q[4]['options'][3]['explanation']='This is an automated policy check if the team chooses it. Major-version distance is not a universal measure of support or security; supported versions and vulnerabilities may be more relevant.'
 q[5]['options'][3]['explanation']='The adapter can reduce call-site changes. Semantic, configuration and operational differences can still make switching costly; it is relatively reversible under suitable assumptions.'
 q[7]['workedExample']=q[7]['workedExample'].replace('most successful microservice stories started as monoliths; many systems built as microservices from scratch ran into trouble.', 'his 2015 essay reports a pattern in stories he had heard, not a statistically representative comparison.').replace('two per person to operate.', 'an average of two services per engineer if divided equally; actual ownership and operational load need not be even.')
 q[8]['options'][0]['explanation']='An architecture diagram alone does not establish ownership or collaboration. Existing technical-team boundaries can continue to require coordination for cross-cutting product changes.'
 q[8]['options'][1]['explanation']='The observation is not defined by a 1,000-person threshold, nor is it a deterministic law about every organization or pair of developers.'
 q[8]['options'][3]['text']='Horizontal ownership can encourage layer-oriented boundaries and cross-team handoffs; cross-functional teams may better support the desired product ownership.'
 q[9]['options'][0]['explanation']='This provides comparison evidence if shadow work has isolated side effects and bounded resource use. Running both can still add production load and differences can contain sensitive data.'
 q[9]['options'][1]['explanation']='Gradual exposure can limit impact. A flag may stop future use, but it cannot undo already-issued prices or incompatible state; test rollback semantics.'
 q[10]['prompt']=q[10]['prompt'].replace('strongest evidence-based concern', 'strongest engineering concern')
 q[10]['workedExample']=q[10]['workedExample'].replace("Spolsky's essay: Netscape spent around three years rewriting its browser, shipping no new major release in that time, while the market moved.", 'Spolsky uses Netscape as an argument about delayed delivery and lost knowledge; this is not proof of a universal rewrite outcome or a verified single-cause chronology.').replace('A rewrite has no value until it\'s complete,', 'A plan that withholds all delivery until completion delays realized value,')
questions(b+'sea-adr-evolution.questions.json',adr,'Qualify incremental rollback, shadow side effects, Conway predictions and historical anecdote strength.',src)
